  "question": {
    "text": "To a 25 mL H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub> solution, excess of acidified solution of potassium iodide was added. The iodine liberated required 20 mL of 0.3 N sodium thiosulphate solution. Calculate the volume strength of H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub> solution and report your answer by multiplying it with 1000.&nbsp;",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1334",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Meq of H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub> = Meq of I<sub>2</sub> = Meq of Na<sub>2</sub>S<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>.&nbsp;<br /><br />If N is normality of H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub>, then<br />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; N x 25 = 0.3 x 20,&nbsp; <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>N</mtext> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <msub> <mtext>O</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </msub> <mo>=</mo> <mn>0</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>2</mn> <mn>4</mn> <mtext>N</mtext> </mrow> </math><br />&nbsp;<br /><math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>M</mtext> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <msub> <mtext>O</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </msub> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>0.12 M</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br />N = 0.24<br /><br />Volume strength = 0.12<math> <mrow> <mo>×</mo> <mtext>11.2</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; =1.334 Vol<br /><br />Final answer <math> <mrow>  <mo>=</mo><mn>1.334</mn><mo>&#x00D7;</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1334</mn></mrow></math>",
